{"audio":{"src":"https://pub-13abeb101e2945d2a7f60234f6faf52e.r2.dev/materials/b1-cologne-perfume-and-the-cathedral-claude/audio/main-f0b626aa4c03.mp3","durationSec":275.784,"cues":[{"start":0,"end":3.08,"text":"Cologne Cathedral stands on a very old religious site."},{"start":3.7,"end":9.36,"text":"After Roman rule ended, Merovingian kings built a church for the bishop there in the 6th century."},{"start":10.14,"end":16.3,"text":"So when work on the Gothic cathedral began on 15 August 1248, the builders were not starting from nothing."},{"start":16.92,"end":19.4,"text":"They were adding a new chapter to a long story."},{"start":20.16,"end":22.64,"text":"The people behind the project were the archbishops."},{"start":23.46,"end":30.2,"text":"They built the cathedral and the city walls to present Cologne as a \"Holy\" city and as the capital of the land they ruled."},{"start":30.82,"end":34.28,"text":"A huge church sent a clear message: this place matters."},{"start":35.08,"end":36.98,"text":"But a message like that costs money."},{"start":37.6,"end":41.92,"text":"Much of the early money came from pilgrims who travelled to visit the Shrine of the Three Kings."},{"start":42.9,"end":46.66,"text":"Think of a popular museum that pays for new rooms with ticket sales."},{"start":47.2,"end":50.54,"text":"The more visitors came, the higher the stone could rise."},{"start":51.14,"end":52.64,"text":"Work moved fast at first."},{"start":53.22,"end":57.72,"text":"The eastern part, called the choir, was finished in 1322."},{"start":58.58,"end":61.22,"text":"Then progress slowed, and finally it stopped."},{"start":62.42,"end":65.82,"text":"You might guess that the building was simply too hard for medieval workers."},{"start":66.52,"end":69.14,"text":"In fact, the reasons were mostly about people and money."},{"start":69.88,"end":71.52,"text":"First, the city had other needs."},{"start":72.26,"end":78.04,"text":"In 1474, the craftsmen were needed to make the city's defences stronger against the Duke of Burgundy."},{"start":78.88,"end":82.14,"text":"A city under threat cares more about walls than towers."},{"start":82.97,"end":85.26,"text":"Second, the money began to disappear."},{"start":86.14,"end":89.4,"text":"By 1473, income from pilgrims had fallen."},{"start":90.18,"end":92.6,"text":"Later, the Reformation and wars made things worse."},{"start":93.44,"end":98.38,"text":"The cathedral lost its money from indulgences, which were special payments collected by the Church."},{"start":98.96,"end":106.84,"text":"Major work stopped in 1473 or 1474, and construction ended completely around 1560."},{"start":107.66,"end":110.58,"text":"The clearest sign of this pause was on the south tower."},{"start":111.34,"end":118,"text":"It was built only up to the level of the bells, and a large crane stayed on top of it for 400 years."},{"start":119.56,"end":124.7,"text":"Generations of people in Cologne grew up looking at an unfinished building with a machine on its head."},{"start":125.6,"end":127.84,"text":"The cathedral was never completely forgotten."},{"start":128.6,"end":135.22,"text":"Efforts to start again began around 1814, and work actually started again in 1823."},{"start":135.96,"end":140.16,"text":"Even so, proper funding arrived only in the 1840s."},{"start":140.68,"end":142.82,"text":"Once again, money decided the speed."},{"start":143.8,"end":146.72,"text":"The 19th-century builders made an important choice."},{"start":147.4,"end":154.6,"text":"They completed the main hall (the nave), the side arms (the transepts) and the towers by following the medieval plans."},{"start":155.02,"end":159.02,"text":"So the finished cathedral is not really a modern building pretending to be old."},{"start":159.46,"end":164.26,"text":"It is closer to an old idea that waited a very long time for the money to finish it."},{"start":164.8,"end":166.66,"text":"This changes the usual question."},{"start":167.38,"end":170.02,"text":"People often ask why the cathedral took so long."},{"start":170.5,"end":174.9,"text":"A better question might be: what kept the plan alive while nothing was being built?"},{"start":177.18,"end":181.24,"text":"Cologne has a second famous symbol, and this one fits in your pocket."},{"start":182.26,"end":189.18,"text":"In 1709, Johann Maria Farina, an Italian, created a perfume from citrus oils and alcohol."},{"start":189.78,"end":193.02,"text":"It was inspired by an Italian spring morning after rain."},{"start":193.76,"end":199.4,"text":"He named it after the city: Eau de Cologne, which means \"water from Cologne\"."},{"start":200.32,"end":201.28,"text":"Notice what happened here."},{"start":201.92,"end":206.28,"text":"The feeling of the perfume came from Italy, but its name came from a German city."},{"start":207.06,"end":211.9,"text":"So every time someone asked for Eau de Cologne, they also said the city's name."},{"start":211.9,"end":214.46,"text":"Famous customers helped the perfume spread."},{"start":215.26,"end":222.1,"text":"Napoleon, the writer Goethe, Queen Victoria and Empress Elisabeth all used Farina's Eau de Cologne."},{"start":222.8,"end":225.7,"text":"Napoleon reportedly used two bottles a day."},{"start":226.5,"end":231.08,"text":"When emperors, queens and great writers choose a product, other people want it too."},{"start":231.84,"end":234.72,"text":"In this way, Cologne became famous for perfume."},{"start":235.58,"end":236.96,"text":"The story has not ended."},{"start":237.7,"end":243.24,"text":"Farina's company, founded in 1709, is the world's oldest fragrance maker."},{"start":243.72,"end":247.04,"text":"Family descendants still make the original Eau de Cologne in the city."},{"start":247.8,"end":257.56,"text":"Its headquarters has been in Farina House since 1723, and today that building is the Fragrance Museum, where visitors can take a 45-minute guided tour."},{"start":258.52,"end":260.36,"text":"Now put the two symbols side by side."},{"start":260.94,"end":263.52,"text":"The cathedral depended on people coming into Cologne."},{"start":264.22,"end":268.36,"text":"Pilgrims brought money, and when that money stopped, the stones stopped too."},{"start":269.14,"end":270.6,"text":"The perfume worked the other way."},{"start":271.02,"end":275.16,"text":"It left the city in bottles and carried Cologne's name to the homes of emperors and queens."}],"words":[{"text":"Cologne","start":0,"end":0.3},{"text":"Cathedral","start":0.3,"end":0.72},{"text":"stands","start":0.72,"end":1.18},{"text":"on","start":1.18,"end":1.42},{"text":"a","start":1.42,"end":1.56},{"text":"very","start":1.56,"end":1.86},{"text":"old","start":1.86,"end":2.28},{"text":"religious","start":2.28,"end":2.64},{"text":"site","start":2.64,"end":3.08},{"text":"After","start":3.7,"end":3.94},{"text":"Roman","start":3.94,"end":4.24},{"text":"rule","start":4.24,"end":4.48},{"text":"ended","start":4.48,"end":4.92},{"text":"Merovingian","start":5.42,"end":5.98},{"text":"kings","start":5.98,"end":6.3},{"text":"built","start":6.3,"end":6.62},{"text":"a","start":6.62,"end":6.84},{"text":"church","start":6.84,"end":7.06},{"text":"for","start":7.06,"end":7.34},{"text":"the","start":7.34,"end":7.48},{"text":"bishop","start":7.48,"end":7.72},{"text":"there","start":7.72,"end":8.06},{"text":"in","start":8.06,"end":8.44},{"text":"the","start":8.44,"end":8.58},{"text":"6th","start":8.58,"end":8.84},{"text":"century","start":8.84,"end":9.36},{"text":"So","start":10.14,"end":10.24},{"text":"when","start":10.24,"end":10.36},{"text":"work","start":10.36,"end":10.6},{"text":"on","start":10.6,"end":10.78},{"text":"the","start":10.78,"end":10.9},{"text":"Gothic","start":10.9,"end":11.22},{"text":"cathedral","start":11.22,"end":11.66},{"text":"began","start":11.66,"end":12.1},{"text":"on","start":12.1,"end":12.36},{"text":"15","start":12.36,"end":12.37},{"text":"August","start":12.36,"end":12.62},{"text":"1248","start":13.4,"end":14},{"text":"the","start":14.54,"end":14.58},{"text":"builders","start":14.58,